    "title": "pandas.Series.T — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.Series.T#\n\n- property Series.T[source]#\n- Return the transpose, which is by definition self. For 1D objects (Series, Index) transposition has no effect; the object is returned unchanged. Provided for API compatibility with DataFrame and NumPy. See also \n  - `Index`\n  - Immutable sequence used for indexing and alignment.\n Examples For Series: >>> s = pd.Series(['Ant', 'Bear', 'Cow']) >>> s 0 Ant 1 Bear 2 Cow dtype: str >>> s.T 0 Ant 1 Bear 2 Cow dtype: str For Index: >>> idx = pd.Index([1, 2, 3]) >>> idx.T Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int64')",
    "markdown_length": 551,
